      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most equitable framework will depend on your city's core values, but generally, prioritizing by income level is the most direct way to address housing inequity. A strict income-based allocation ensures that the units go to those who need them most, directly combating economic displacement. While lotteries offer randomness, they ignore the urgent need of low-income residents, and transit proximity alone doesn't guarantee affordability for the neediest.",
      "source": "target",
